-## Initialisation and Privacy
-
-- `init` creates a bounded, deterministic, non-semantic baseline from verified root package metadata, a bounded root directory snapshot, and workflow filenames. It does not traverse source directories or generate language counts or regular-file totals; agents may discover these separately.
-- Every baseline directory source reads at most 513 raw entries before filtering and is bound to a stable real-directory generation. Only the root and `.github/workflows` are enumerated; workflow ancestry and all retained baseline sources must share a stable repository-root generation. The package pass always opens the literal root `package.json`; exact casing wins when case-distinct aliases coexist, while an enumerated alias supplies attribution only when that literal open succeeds on a case-insensitive filesystem. Validated top-level presence distinguishes a package or `.github` source that disappears before its preliminary metadata check from ordinary absence. Overflow, unreadable directories, workflow enumeration failures, and invalid, oversized, or stably unreadable package metadata omit the affected facts and set `scanTruncated` with bounded, ordinal-sorted reason codes in the repository overview. Package replacement or other source change discards the complete attempt instead.
-- Baseline payload assembly retains compact root, directory, package-content, absence, and expected-failure evidence and revalidates all of it together before acceptance. A changed attempt is discarded in full and retried within one baseline-owned ledger of at most three complete attempts and one non-resetting 60-second deadline, checked before a retry. Stable expected failures retain their deterministic truncation reasons; persistent churn returns concise path-free `REPOSITORY_CHANGED`.
-- The complete baseline reason vocabulary is `package-metadata-error`, `top-level-entry-limit`, `unreadable-directory`, `workflow-entry-limit`, and `workflow-enumeration-error`.
-- The generated overview contains `recognisedTopLevelFiles`, `topLevelDirectories`, `sources`, `summary`, `scanTruncated`, and `scanTruncationReasons`. Tooling and command records retain their existing package, workspace, manager, script-argv, and workflow fields. The existing JSON search projection indexes these retained facts; init adds no separate source inventory or search text.
