+## Package and Release Gates
+
+- The working package version remains 0.3.0 until the release ticket. The immutable published compatibility oracle is encephalon@0.3.0; candidate filenames derive from the validated working package version.
+- The exact candidate artifact is the fixed retained tarball plus its metadata sidecar; every downstream gate recomputes that identity before use.
+- Runtime consumers require Node.js 24.15.0 or newer and do not require Bun.
+- The npm package has no runtime dependencies and no install, preinstall, postinstall, or prepare lifecycle scripts. The package gate rejects `dependencies`, `optionalDependencies`, `peerDependencies`, `peerDependenciesMeta`, `bundledDependencies`, and `bundleDependencies` when present, while development dependencies remain permitted.
+- `bun run check:generated` is contributor convenience for trusted local checkouts. Its target generated-version checker is non-mutating, but package lifecycle hooks and Bun preloads mean the alias is not an authority for untrusted changes. Every source-building CI job must instead run the exact direct command `node ./scripts/check-generated-version.ts` immediately after Node setup and before Bun setup or installation so those hooks and preloads cannot run first. The check compares the complete committed package-version source; stale or missing source receives deterministic build-and-commit guidance, while unrelated I/O failures remain unchanged.
+- The tarball manifest is intentionally small and checked by `bun run check:package`. Every packed path must be either a reviewed tracked package input, the public declaration facade, or a runtime file reachable through the API/CLI entrypoints. Static and lazy imports must resolve to contained package files or Node built-ins. The packed manifest is validated independently, and every packed file's mode and bytes must exactly equal the reviewed source or build output; untracked source-tree files, altered content, private declarations, and extra generated outputs fail before candidate execution or retention.
+- The synchronous root API and CLI share one ESM implementation graph. CLI help/version and invalid command options load only the parser and its error, budget, and version support; command implementations load after CLI argument validation. The package exposes only its root API and public declaration facade. Maintainer performance documents remain in Git and are excluded from npm.
+- The release gate or contributor must build before `bun run check:package`; without arguments the package check creates and validates one tarball, while `--tarball <repository-relative-path>` validates an existing exact `.tgz` without invoking `npm pack`. Both modes install only a private snapshot into temporary Git repositories with scripts disabled, import the API, typecheck the complete public declaration consumer, execute the packed CLI through Node, and exercise literal result limits 50, 100, 101, 999, 1,000, and the exact 1,001 rejection for list, full search, compact search, and gather. Its opt-in retained tarball is installed only after every package check passes. Descriptor-bound reads, stable ancestor identities, exclusive installation, and a final rehash require it to remain byte-identical to the reviewed snapshot.
+- Exact retention also creates `package-artifacts/encephalon-<version>.tgz.metadata.json`, the bounded deterministic metadata sidecar authority for byte size, SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-512, npm integrity, package version, source commit, and the fixed repository-relative tarball path. Retention requires `package-artifacts` to be absent, stages the complete pair in one random private sibling under the stable reviewed repository root, installs the whole directory with one rename, and revalidates directory/file identities and every digest. A previous disposable artifact directory must be moved aside before regeneration; callers never merge with or replace it. Supplied checks, candidate jobs, release jobs, compatibility, and the publish dry run independently run the shared fixed-path preflight, bind the sidecar to current `package.json` and `HEAD`, and validate packed bytes against the reviewed source/build before using the tarball. Supplied and retained paths are mutually exclusive, repository-relative, single-linked regular files or safe directories as applicable, and cannot traverse or replace an ancestor.
+- `bun run check:compatibility <repository-relative-candidate.tgz>` is the release-only upgrade and downgrade gate. It snapshots the supplied candidate through the package-tarball authority, requires its manifest version to equal the reviewed source release, downloads `encephalon@0.3.0` with lifecycle scripts disabled, and verifies the published tarball's pinned SHA-1 and npm SHA-512 integrity before installation or execution. Oracle/candidate snapshots, trusted probes, install stages, npm cache, and the candidate fixture use independent private roots. Every artifact and installed package tree retains canonical path, device, inode, hard-link count, type, mode, byte, root, and parent-generation witnesses; hashes and identities are rechecked immediately before every install or invocation. Each package transition uses a fresh staged install, atomically places that exact tree, retires the predecessor without recursively deleting candidate-controlled children, and protects the installed tree around every phase. Complete bounded fixture snapshots surround every import, declaration, API, CLI, and budget phase, with only explicit canonical initialisation and disposable-cache mutations allowed; unrelated files and `package.json` changes fail. Trusted serialisation/stdout intrinsics and an allowlisted child environment are captured before candidate import. A trusted supervisor bounds output/time, terminates the complete process tree on timeout or cancellation, and waits for reaping before post-process snapshots. Cleanup traversals are bounded, do not follow symlinks, and dispose only identity-matched isolated roots. Fresh Node processes then exercise declarations, every public API and CLI command, exact successful values and error envelopes, help/version output, the complete 50/100/101/999/1,000/1,001 result-limit table, the byte and term boundaries for full search, compact search, and every gather search path, every independent gather-array, supersession, payload, corpus, and response-byte boundary, aggregate corpus supersession and artifact ceilings, candidate payload allocation order and retained work, and cache schema 2→4→2 recovery in one temporary Git repository. Stable public values are compared exactly after normalising temporary-root paths, generated timestamps, and the literal package version. During upgrade only, compact-search and gathered-search rank/snippet values may change: ranks must remain finite, snippets must remain non-empty and at most 1,100 UTF-8 bytes, and all other fields, shapes, identities, and order remain exact for the compatibility fixture. Downgrade still compares the complete historical values exactly. Candidate help must equal the published 0.3 help exactly. Both versions accept 1–1,000 results and reject 1,001 with the same budget, field and maximum details. Independent candidate budget boundaries remain exact, and downgrade must reproduce the oracle's original evidence. Canonical records, referenced artifacts, and managed `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` complete permission modes, durable identities, and bytes must remain identical in both directions. Success writes one deterministic JSON report containing both package digests, normalised public-surface digests, independent-budget evidence, and both transition results. The explicit historical release-tool suite uses local stand-in tarballs and does not contact npm; ordinary source tests do not construct those fixtures.
+- Compatibility evidence is derived only from public candidate behaviour. The allocation probe installs reflection instrumentation around public `addRecord` calls before and after package import, while aggregate supersession and artifact evidence comes only from public API/CLI validation over generated temporary canonical fixtures. A candidate-supplied export or other non-public witness is never accepted as release evidence.
+- `bun run check:publish <repository-relative-tarball>` is a tarball-only dry-run release gate. It passes that exact validated `.tgz` as npm's publish target and never publishes or dry-runs the source directory. Publishing is manual maintainer work and must not be performed by agents. An already-published version is accepted only when npm terminates normally with exit code `1`, every structured or explicit failure diagnostic is the expected conflict, and no unrelated fatal diagnostic is present. The package and publish contributor commands launch Node scripts; CI invokes those scripts directly and supplies its retained candidate path so package lifecycle hooks and Bun preloads cannot run at the validation boundary.
+- Every authoritative package or publish Node step that runs after Bun setup explicitly clears `NODE_OPTIONS` and `NODE_PATH`, including for child npm and Node processes, so an earlier untrusted lifecycle or build step cannot preload code into the validation boundary.
+- CI runs the complete build-independent source suite on Linux at minimum/current Node versions, with lint, types and cheap tool tests before one explicit package build. An explicit exhaustive test-file classification retains filesystem/path/process coverage on macOS and Windows; changed source-only test files also run there. Unknown, duplicate or stale classifications fail. Package-dependent tests run after restoring the selected artifact, including installed CLI and executable coverage on all three operating systems. `test:all` retains the full local suite, with `test:history` available independently.
+- The producer checks tracked and untracked cleanliness before and after building and requires an absent artifact directory. It emits the exact immutable GitHub artifact ID, version-derived relative tarball path and independently recorded SHA-256. Consumers download that ID, verify all sidecar identities against the checked-out source and external digest, restore only the reviewed flat runtime/declaration files into an absent `dist`, then use the existing strict package preflight. They never build source or repack the candidate. Consumer-only reruns use the original producer outputs; full reruns select a new attempt-specific artifact.
+- Real published 0.3 compatibility runs for every main candidate and every PR affecting production, public/persisted formats, package contents, build or release behaviour. Known ordinary docs/test-only PRs may skip it; unknown paths, removed files and both rename paths are conservative. Historical release-tool regressions run on relevant tool/CI changes. A `release` label, manual main run and weekly main schedule force both gates. Main compatibility is unconditional because a preceding relevant run may have been cancelled. Selection failures fail the required gate; only explicitly unselected history may be skipped.
+- The six Linux performance shards retain the common 20 measured plus two warmup samples per operation and side. Benchmark smoke and publish dry-run consumers use the selected candidate. PR CI remains read-only and receives no repository, provider or npm secrets. No job publishes to npm.
+- The final gate retains `verified-candidate-<attempt>` only after all selected checks succeed. A separate `workflow_run` workflow promotes only an already completed, successful, same-repository main CI run triggered by push, schedule or manual dispatch. Promotion executes no repository or candidate code and only copies the verified artifact. The trusted name includes source SHA, originating run and attempt. Superseded PR/main work is cancelled; cancelled or failed CI cannot promote. Before the manual explicit-approval tarball-only publish handoff, require current-main identity and byte equality with the reviewed PR candidate.
+
+Branch protection retains `verify (ubuntu-latest)`, `verify (macos-latest)`, `verify (windows-latest)`, `verify (ubuntu-current)`, `Release-equivalent package gate` and `Greptile Review`. Greptile must report 5/5 for the reviewed head. Re-query the read-only status-check configuration with:
+
+```bash
+gh api repos/isaachinman/encephalon/branches/main/protection/required_status_checks \
+  --jq '{strict, contexts: (.contexts | sort)}'
+```
